<h1>Experiments</h1>
<p>A sandbox page for a few elements that don&rsquo;t belong anywhere in the actual
  portfolio narrative: <code>&lt;template&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;audio&gt;</code>,
  <code>&lt;video&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;math&gt;</code>.</p>

<section>
  <h2>The same element, configured differently</h2>
  <p>This is the identical <code>&lt;quake-feed&gt;</code> element from the home
    page, given different attributes: significant quakes over the past week rather
    than magnitude 2.5 and up over the past day. Nothing about the element changes
    &mdash; only its markup.</p>
  <quake-feed magnitude="significant" period="week" count="10">
    <p>Significant earthquakes from the past week are loaded from the U.S. Geological
      Survey and need JavaScript to display. The same feed is browsable at
      <a href="https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/map/">earthquake.usgs.gov</a>.</p>
  </quake-feed>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Template</h2>
  <p>The <code>&lt;template&gt;</code> element below is inert &mdash; its contents are
    parsed but never rendered unless something clones them. Nothing on this page
    does. It is the same mechanism the earthquake element above uses to build each
    list item safely.</p>
  <template id="card-template">
    <article class="tpl-card">
      <h3>Card title</h3>
      <p>Card body text goes here.</p>
    </article>
  </template>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Audio</h2>
  <audio controls>
    <source src="/assets/sample-audio.mp3" type="audio/mpeg">
    <source src="/assets/sample-audio.ogg" type="audio/ogg">
    Your browser doesn&rsquo;t support the audio element. Here&rsquo;s a
    <a href="/assets/sample-audio.mp3">direct link to the file</a> instead.
  </audio>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Video</h2>
