</section>

<section>
  <h2>MathML</h2>
  <p>Mass-energy equivalence, written with native <code>&lt;math&gt;</code> markup:</p>
  <math display="block">
    <mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup>
  </math>
  <p>MathML has been around since the late 1990s, but Chrome didn&rsquo;t get native
    support until <b>Chrome 109</b> in January 2023 &mdash; Firefox and Safari had it
    for years before that. A good reminder to check
    <a href="https://caniuse.com/mathml" target="_blank" rel="noopener">caniuse.com</a>
    before leaning on a feature like this.</p>
</section>
